The graph shows the possum population of a reserve over $18$ months, with the mean position drawn as a dashed line. Which model gives the population $P$ after $t$ months?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[width=10cm,height=6.5cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=-0.6,xmax=19.6,ymin=0,ymax=1650,xtick={0,2,...,18},ytick={0,200,...,1600},grid=both,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\small,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={$t$ (months)},ylabel={Population},ylabel near ticks]
\addplot[thick,blue!70!black,domain=0:18,samples=150] {400*cos(20*x)+1000};
\addplot[dashed,domain=0:18,samples=2] {1000};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
